1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:11,800
♪ 'Twas brillig, and the slithy toves ♪
♪ Did gyre and gimble in the wabe; ♪

2
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:23,100
♪ All mimsy were the borogoves, ♪
♪ And the mome raths outgrabe. ♪

3
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:34,200
♪ "Beware the Jabberwock, my son! ♪
♪ The jaws that bite, the claws that catch! ♪

4
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:45,400
♪ Beware the Jubjub bird, and shun ♪
♪ The frumious Bandersnatch!" ♪

5
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:56,500
♪ He took his vorpal sword in hand: ♪
♪ Long time the manxome foe he sought— ♪

6
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:07,900
♪ So rested he by the Tumtum tree, ♪
♪ And stood awhile in thought. ♪

7
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:19,000
♪ And as in uffish thought he stood, ♪
♪ The Jabberwock, with eyes of flame, ♪

8
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:30,200
♪ Came whiffling through the tulgey wood, ♪
♪ And burbled as it came! ♪

9
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:41,500
♪ One, two! One, two! And through and through ♪
♪ The vorpal blade went snicker-snack! ♪

10
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:58,500
♪ He left it dead, and with its head ♪
♪ He went galumphing back. ♪

11
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,900
(Alice-chan) A mad tea-party...

12
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,200
There was a table set out under a tree in front of the house.

13
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:12,400
The March Hare-san and the Hatter-san were having tea at it.

14
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,700
A Dormouse-san was sitting between them, fast asleep.

15
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:21,500
The other two were using it as a cushion, resting their elbows on it.

16
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:25,900
They were talking right over its head.

17
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,800
*Very uncomfortable for the Dormouse-san...*

18
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:32,900
Only, as it's asleep, I suppose it doesn't mind.

19
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:36,800
The table was a large one, but the three were all crowded together at one corner of it.

20
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:39,500
No room! No room!

21
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:42,500
There's plenty of room!

22
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,400
She sat down in a large arm-chair at one end of the table.

23
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,900
Have some wine.

24
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:51,900
I don't see any wine.

25
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:54,200
There isn't any.

26
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:57,900
Then it wasn't very civil of you to offer it.

27
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,800
It wasn't very civil of you to sit down without being invited.